# Files that run or are parsed inside Linux containers must keep LF endings, even on a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF shebang ("#!/bin/sh\r") makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "sh\r", which fails as "not found".
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.envsh         text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
